From: Herman van Hazendonk <github.com@herrie.org>
Date: Sat, 26 Sep 2026 00:00:00 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] input: kpd_customkey: release the wakeup source unconditionally

The FLX1s privacy switches (cam_switch on GPIO 51, nwk_switch on GPIO 52)
are handled by this driver. Every edge takes a wakeup source and schedules
delayed_sleep_work_fn() to drop it again WAKEUP_HOLD_MS later, so userspace
gets a chance to react before the system is allowed to suspend.

The release was guarded by a file-scope "gpio_value", set from whichever key
fired last:

	if(gpio_value)
		__pm_relax(data->ws);
	printk(KERN_INFO "Wake lock released after %d ms gpio_value:%d\n", ...);

That is wrong twice over.

One, the variable is a single global shared by every key the DT describes,
so two switches racing each other decide one another's release. Two, and
worse, when the last edge left the GPIO low the guard is false and
__pm_relax() is never reached at all - the wakeup source stays active for
the rest of the uptime and the system can no longer suspend. The printk
claims otherwise regardless of what happened, which is how this hides:

	[78298.855215] Wake lock released after 3000 ms gpio_value:1
	[78310.119112] Wake lock released after 3000 ms gpio_value:0   <- leaked

Both switches idle with their GPIO low, so a single flip of either one is
enough to pin the device awake, and the message in dmesg says it was
released.

There is no reason to make the release conditional: the hold is a fixed
timeout, not a level. Drop the guard, and with it the shared global, which
has no other user. __pm_relax() on an already inactive source is harmless,
so the unguarded call is safe on every path.

Observed on a FuriPhone FLX1s (MT6877) running LuneOS.

kpd_customkey.c is an ODM driver that exists only in FuriLabs' vendor tree
(it arrived in "Import ODM changes", 1f9da8203452), so there is no kernel.org
upstream to send this to - but it is worth offering to FuriLabs, since FuriOS
runs the same driver on the same switches and has the same leak.


Not-signed-off: add your own Signed-off-by before sending this to FuriLabs.

Signed-off-by: Herman van Hazendonk <github.com@herrie.org>
Upstream-Status: Inappropriate [ODM driver, exists only in the vendor tree]
---
--- a/drivers/input/keyboard/kpd_customkey.c
+++ b/drivers/input/keyboard/kpd_customkey.c
@@ -58,7 +58,6 @@
 };
 struct gpio_keys_data *gData = NULL;
 
-static int gpio_value = 1;
 static ssize_t key_state_show(struct device *dev, 
                              struct device_attribute *attr, 
                              char *buf) {
@@ -78,10 +77,9 @@
     struct gpio_keys_data *data = container_of(to_delayed_work(work), 
                                              struct gpio_keys_data, sleep_work);
 
-    if(gpio_value)
-	__pm_relax(data->ws);
+    __pm_relax(data->ws);
 
-    printk(KERN_INFO "Wake lock released after %d ms gpio_value:%d\n", WAKEUP_HOLD_MS,gpio_value);
+    printk(KERN_INFO "Wake lock released after %d ms\n", WAKEUP_HOLD_MS);
 }
 
 static irqreturn_t key_irq_handler(int irq, void *dev_id) {
@@ -98,7 +96,6 @@
     __pm_stay_awake(data->ws);
 
     value = gpio_get_value(key->gpio);
-    gpio_value = value;
     mutex_lock(&data->lock);
     key->pressed = (value ? 0 : 1);
     mutex_unlock(&data->lock);
